Rem ===================================================================
Rem cave-messages.shoddy -- what the cave says. Hand-edited source.
Rem First written by a generator from adventure.yaml; both are in
Rem obsolete/ now and neither is run. The C is the reference.
Rem
Rem 213 arbitrary messages, in declaration order.
Rem Messages() is indexed from zero, matching rspeak(n) in the C.
Rem The Msg* words below give every message its name back.
Rem ===================================================================

Def Messages() As List Of String
    {
      Rem 0  NO_MESSAGE
      "",

      Rem 1  CAVE_NEARBY
          "Somewhere nearby is Colossal Cave, where others have found fortunes in\n"
        & "treasure and gold, though it is rumored that some who enter are never\n"
        & "seen again.  Magic is said to work in the cave.  I will be your eyes\n"
        & "and hands.  Direct me with commands of 1 or 2 words.  I should warn\n"
        & "you that I look at only the first five letters of each word, so you'll\n"
        & "have to enter \"northeast\" as \"ne\" to distinguish it from \"north\".\n"
        & "You can type \"help\" for some general hints.  For information on how\n"
        & "to end your adventure, scoring, etc., type \"info\".\n"
        & "\t\t\t      - - -\n"
        & "This program was originally developed by Willie Crowther.  Most of the\n"
        & "features of the current program were added by Don Woods.",

      Rem 2  CURMUDGEON_BLOCK
      "A little curmudgeon with a big knife blocks your way.",

      Rem 3  CURMUDGEON_RAN
          "A little curmudgeon just walked around a corner, saw you, threw a\n"
        & "little axe at you which missed, cursed, and ran away.",

      Rem 4  CURMUDGEON_PACK
      "There are %d threatening little curmudgeons in the room with you.",

      Rem 5  CURMUDGEON_SINGLE
      "There is a threatening little curmudgeon in the room with you!",

      Rem 6  KNIFE_THROWN
      "One sharp nasty knife is thrown at you!",

      Rem 7  SAYS_PLUGH
      "A hollow voice says \"PLUGH\".",

      Rem 8  GETS_YOU
      "It gets you!",

      Rem 9  MISSES_YOU
      "It misses!",

      Rem 10  UNSURE_FACING
      "I am unsure how you are facing.  Use compass points or nearby objects.",

      Rem 11  NO_INOUT_HERE
          "I don't know in from out here.  Use compass points or name something\n"
        & "in the general direction you want to go.",

      Rem 12  CANT_APPLY
      "I don't know how to apply that word here.",

      Rem 13  AM_GAME
      "I'm game.  Would you care to explain how?",

      Rem 14  NO_MORE_DETAIL
          "Sorry, but I am not allowed to give more detail.  I will repeat the\n"
        & "long description of your location.",

      Rem 15  PITCH_DARK
      "It is now pitch dark.  If you proceed you will likely fall into a pit.",

      Rem 16  W_IS_WEST
      "If you prefer, simply type w rather than west.",

      Rem 17  REALLY_QUIT
      "Do you really want to quit now?",

      Rem 18  PIT_FALL
      "You fell into a pit and broke every bone in your body!",

      Rem 19  ALREADY_CARRYING
      "You are already carrying it!",

      Rem 20  YOU_JOKING
      "You can't be serious!",

      Rem 21  BIRD_EVADES
          "The bird seemed unafraid at first, but as you approach it becomes\n"
        & "disturbed and you cannot catch it.",

      Rem 22  CANNOT_CARRY
      "You can catch the bird, but you cannot carry it.",

      Rem 23  NOTHING_LOCKED
      "There is nothing here with a lock!",

      Rem 24  ARENT_CARRYING
      "You aren't carrying it!",

      Rem 25  BIRD_ATTACKS
          "The little bird attacks the green snake, and in an astounding flurry\n"
        & "drives the snake away.",

      Rem 26  NO_KEYS
      "You have no keys!",

      Rem 27  NO_LOCK
      "It has no lock.",

      Rem 28  NOT_LOCKABLE
      "I don't know how to lock or unlock such a thing.",

      Rem 29  ALREADY_LOCKED
      "It was already locked.",

      Rem 30  ALREADY_UNLOCKED
      "It was already unlocked.",

      Rem 31  BEAR_BLOCKS
          "There is no way to get past the bear to unlock the chain, which is\n"
        & "probably just as well.",

      Rem 32  NOTHING_HAPPENS
      "Nothing happens.",

      Rem 33  WHERE_QUERY
      "Where?",

      Rem 34  NO_TARGET
      "There is nothing here to attack.",

      Rem 35  BIRD_DEAD
      "The little bird is now dead.  Its body disappears.",

      Rem 36  SNAKE_WARNING
      "Attacking the snake both doesn't work and is very dangerous.",

      Rem 37  KILLED_CURMUDGEON
      "You killed a little curmudgeon.",

      Rem 38  CURMUDGEON_DODGES
      "You attack a little curmudgeon, but he dodges out of the way.",

      Rem 39  BARE_HANDS_QUERY
      "With what?  Your bare hands?",

      Rem 40  BAD_DIRECTION
      "There is no way to go that direction.",

      Rem 41  TWO_WORDS
      "Please stick to 1- and 2-word commands.",

      Rem 42  OK_MAN
      "OK",

      Rem 43  CANNOT_UNLOCK
      "You can't unlock the keys.",

      Rem 44  FUTILE_CRAWL
          "You have crawled around in some little holes and wound up back in the\n"
        & "main passage.",

      Rem 45  FOLLOW_STREAM
          "I don't know where the cave is, but hereabouts no stream can run on\n"
        & "the surface for long.  I would try the stream.",

      Rem 46  NEED_DETAIL
      "I need more detailed instructions to do that.",

      Rem 47  NEARBY
          "I can only tell you what you see as you move about and manipulate\n"
        & "things.  I cannot tell you where remote things are.",

      Rem 48  OGRE_SNARL
      "The ogre snarls and shoves you back.",

      Rem 49  HUH_MAN
      "Huh?",

      Rem 50  WELCOME_YOU
      "Welcome to Adventure!!  Would you like instructions?",

      Rem 51  REQUIRES_DYNAMITE
      "Blasting requires dynamite.",

      Rem 52  FEET_WET
      "Your feet are now wet.",

      Rem 53  LOST_APPETITE
      "I think I just lost my appetite.",

      Rem 54  THANKS_DELICIOUS
      "Thank you, it was delicious!",

      Rem 55  PECULIAR_NOTHING
      "Peculiar.  Nothing unexpected happens.",

      Rem 56  GROUND_WET
      "Your bottle is empty and the ground is wet.",

      Rem 57  CANT_POUR
      "You can't pour that.",

      Rem 58  WHICH_WAY
      "Which way?",

      Rem 59  FORGOT_PATH
      "Sorry, but I no longer seem to remember how it was you got here.",

      Rem 60  CARRY_LIMIT
      "You can't carry anything more.  You'll have to drop something first.",

      Rem 61  GRATE_NOWAY
      "You can't go through a locked steel grate!",

      Rem 62  YOU_HAVEIT
      "I believe what you want is right here with you.",

      Rem 63  DONT_FIT
      "You don't fit through a two-inch slit!",

      Rem 64  CROSS_BRIDGE
      "I respectfully suggest you go across the bridge instead of jumping.",

      Rem 65  NO_CROSS
      "There is no way across the fissure.",

      Rem 66  NO_CARRY
      "You're not carrying anything.",

      Rem 67  NOW_HOLDING
      "You are currently holding the following:",

      Rem 68  BIRD_PINING
          "It's not hungry (it's merely pinin' for the fjords).  Besides, you\n"
        & "have no bird seed.",

      Rem 69  BIRD_DEVOURED
      "The snake has now devoured your bird.",

      Rem 70  NOTHING_EDIBLE
      "There's nothing here it wants to eat (except perhaps you).",

      Rem 71  REALLY_MAD
      "You fool, curmudgeons eat only coal!  Now you've made him *REALLY* mad!!",

      Rem 72  NO_CONTAINER
      "You have nothing in which to carry it.",

      Rem 73  BOTTLE_FULL
      "Your bottle is already full.",

      Rem 74  NO_LIQUID
      "There is nothing here with which to fill the bottle.",

      Rem 75  RIDICULOUS_ATTEMPT
      "Don't be ridiculous!",

      Rem 76  RUSTY_DOOR
      "The door is extremely rusty and refuses to open.",

      Rem 77  SHAKING_LEAVES
      "The plant indignantly shakes the oil off its leaves and asks, \"Water?\"",

      Rem 78  DEEP_ROOTS
      "The plant has exceptionally deep roots and cannot be pulled free.",

      Rem 79  KNIVES_VANISH
      "The curmudgeons' knives vanish as they strike the walls of the cave.",

      Rem 80  MUST_DROP
          "Something you're carrying won't fit through the tunnel with you.\n"
        & "You'd best take inventory and drop something.",

      Rem 81  CLAM_BLOCKER
      "You can't fit this five-foot clam through that little passage!",

      Rem 82  OYSTER_BLOCKER
      "You can't fit this five-foot oyster through that little passage!",

      Rem 83  DROP_CLAM
      "I advise you to put down the clam before opening it.  >STRAIN!<",

      Rem 84  DROP_OYSTER
      "I advise you to put down the oyster before opening it.  >WRENCH!<",

      Rem 85  CLAM_OPENER
      "You don't have anything strong enough to open the clam.",

      Rem 86  OYSTER_OPENER
      "You don't have anything strong enough to open the oyster.",

      Rem 87  PEARL_FALLS
          "A glistening pearl falls out of the clam and rolls away.  Goodness,\n"
        & "this must really be an oyster.  (I never was very good at identifying\n"
        & "bivalves.)  Whatever it is, it has now snapped shut again.",

      Rem 88  OYSTER_OPENS
          "The oyster creaks open, revealing nothing but oyster inside.  It\n"
        & "promptly snaps shut again.",

      Rem 89  WAY_BLOCKED
          "You have crawled around in some little holes and found your way\n"
        & "blocked by a recent cave-in.  You are now back in the main passage.",

      Rem 90  PIRATE_RUSTLES
      "There are faint rustling noises from the darkness behind you.",

      Rem 91  PIRATE_POUNCES
          "Out from the shadows behind you pounces a bearded pirate!  \"Har, har,\"\n"
        & "he chortles, \"I'll just take all this booty and hide it away with me\n"
        & "chest deep in the maze!\"  He snatches your treasure and vanishes into\n"
        & "the gloom.",

      Rem 92  CAVE_CLOSING
          "A sepulchral voice reverberating through the cave, says, \"Cave closing\n"
        & "soon.  All adventurers exit immediately through main office.\"",

      Rem 93  EXIT_CLOSED
          "A mysterious recorded voice groans into life and announces:\n"
        & "   \"This exit is closed.  Please leave via main office.\"",

      Rem 94  DEATH_CLOSING
          "It looks as though you're dead.  Well, seeing as how it's so close to\n"
        & "closing time anyway, I think we'll just call it a day.",

      Rem 95  CAVE_CLOSED
          "The sepulchral voice intones, \"The cave is now closed.\"  As the echoes\n"
        & "fade, there is a blinding flash of light (and a small puff of orange\n"
        & "smoke). . . .    As your eyes refocus, you look around and find...",

      Rem 96  VICTORY_MESSAGE
          "There is a loud explosion, and a twenty-foot hole appears in the far\n"
        & "wall, burying the curmudgeons in the rubble.  You march through the\n"
        & "hole and find yourself in the main office, where a cheering band of\n"
        & "friendly elves carry the conquering adventurer off into the sunset.",

      Rem 97  DEFEAT_MESSAGE
          "There is a loud explosion, and a twenty-foot hole appears in the far\n"
        & "wall, burying the snakes in the rubble.  A river of molten lava pours\n"
        & "in through the hole, destroying everything in its path, including you!",

      Rem 98  SPLATTER_MESSAGE
          "There is a loud explosion, and you are suddenly splashed across the\n"
        & "walls of the room.",

      Rem 99  CURMUDGEONS_AWAKEN
          "The resulting ruckus has awakened the curmudgeons.  There are now\n"
        & "several threatening little curmudgeons in the room with you!  Most of\n"
        & "them throw knives at you!  All of them get you!",

      Rem 100  UNHAPPY_BIRD
      "Oh, leave the poor unhappy bird alone.",

      Rem 101  NEEDED_NEARBY
      "I daresay whatever you want is around here somewhere.",

      Rem 102  NOT_CONNECTED
      "You can't get there from here.",

      Rem 103  TAME_BEAR
      "You are being followed by a very large, tame bear.",

      Rem 104  WITHOUT_SUSPENDS
      "Now let's see you do it without suspending in mid-Adventure.",

      Rem 105  FILL_INVALID
      "There is nothing here with which to fill it.",

      Rem 106  SHATTER_VASE
      "The sudden change in temperature has delicately shattered the vase.",

      Rem 107  BEYOND_POWER
      "It is beyond your power to do that.",

      Rem 108  NOT_KNOWHOW
      "I don't know how.",

      Rem 109  TOO_FAR
      "It is too far up for you to reach.",

      Rem 110  CURMUDGEON_SMOKE
          "You killed a little curmudgeon.  The body vanishes in a cloud of\n"
        & "greasy black smoke.",

      Rem 111  SHELL_IMPERVIOUS
      "The shell is very strong and is impervious to attack.",

      Rem 112  START_OVER
      "What's the matter, can't you read?  Now you'd best start over.",

      Rem 113  WELL_POINTLESS
      "Well, that was remarkably pointless!",

      Rem 114  DRAGON_SCALES
      "The axe bounces harmlessly off the dragon's thick scales.",

      Rem 115  NASTY_DRAGON
      "The dragon looks rather nasty.  You'd best not try to get by.",

      Rem 116  BIRD_BURNT
          "The little bird attacks the green dragon, and in an astounding flurry\n"
        & "gets burnt to a cinder.  The ashes blow away.",

      Rem 117  BRIEF_CONFIRM
          "Okay, from now on I'll only describe a place in full the first time\n"
        & "you come to it.  To get the full description, say \"look\".",

      Rem 118  ROCKY_TROLL
          "Trolls are close relatives with the rocks and have skin as tough as\n"
        & "that of a rhinoceros.  The troll fends off your blows effortlessly.",

      Rem 119  TROLL_RETURNS
          "The troll deftly catches the axe, examines it carefully, and tosses it\n"
        & "back, declaring, \"Good workmanship, but it's not valuable enough.\"",

      Rem 120  TROLL_SATISFIED
      "The troll catches your treasure and scurries away out of sight.",

      Rem 121  TROLL_BLOCKS
      "The troll refuses to let you cross.",

      Rem 122  BRIDGE_GONE
      "There is no longer any way across the chasm.",

      Rem 123  BEAR_HANDS
      "With what?  Your bare hands?  Against *HIS* bear hands??",

      Rem 124  BEAR_CONFUSED
      "The bear is confused; he only wants to be your friend.",

      Rem 125  ALREADY_DEAD
      "For crying out loud, the poor thing is already dead!",

      Rem 126  BEAR_CHAINED
      "The bear is still chained to the wall.",

      Rem 127  STILL_LOCKED
      "The chain is still locked.",

      Rem 128  CHAIN_UNLOCKED
      "The chain is now unlocked.",

      Rem 129  CHAIN_LOCKED
      "The chain is now locked.",

      Rem 130  NO_LOCKSITE
      "There is nothing here to which the chain can be locked.",

      Rem 131  WANT_HINT
      "Do you want the hint?",

      Rem 132  TROLL_VICES
      "Gluttony is not one of the troll's vices.  Avarice, however, is.",

      Rem 133  LAMP_DIM
          "Your lamp is getting dim.  You'd best start wrapping this up, unless\n"
        & "you can find some fresh batteries.  I seem to recall there's a vending\n"
        & "machine in the maze.  Bring some coins with you.",

      Rem 134  LAMP_OUT
      "Your lamp has run out of power.",

      Rem 135  PLEASE_ANSWER
      "Please answer the question.",

      Rem 136  PIRATE_SPOTTED
          "There are faint rustling noises from the darkness behind you.  As you\n"
        & "turn toward them, the beam of your lamp falls across a bearded pirate.\n"
        & "He is carrying a large chest.  \"Shiver me timbers!\" he cries, \"I've\n"
        & "been spotted!  I'd best hie meself off to the maze to hide me chest!\"\n"
        & "With that, he vanishes into the gloom.",

      Rem 137  GET_BATTERIES
      "Your lamp is getting dim.  You'd best go back for those batteries.",

      Rem 138  REPLACE_BATTERIES
          "Your lamp is getting dim.  I'm taking the liberty of replacing the\n"
        & "batteries.",

      Rem 139  MISSING_BATTERIES
          "Your lamp is getting dim, and you're out of spare batteries.  You'd\n"
        & "best start wrapping this up.",

      Rem 140  REMOVE_MESSAGE
          "You sift your fingers through the dust, but succeed only in\n"
        & "obliterating the cryptic message.",

      Rem 141  CLUE_QUERY
          "Hmmm, this looks like a clue, which means it'll cost you 10 points to\n"
        & "read it.  Should I go ahead and read it anyway?",

      Rem 142  WAYOUT_CLUE
          "It says, \"There is a way out of this place.  Do you need any more\n"
        & "information to escape?  Sorry, but this initial hint is all you get.\"",

      Rem 143  DONT_UNDERSTAND
      "I'm afraid I don't understand.",

      Rem 144  HAND_PASSTHROUGH
      "Your hand passes through it as though it weren't there.",

      Rem 145  PROD_CURMUDGEON
          "You prod the nearest curmudgeon, who wakes up grumpily, takes one look\n"
        & "at you, curses, and grabs for his axe.",

      Rem 146  THIS_ACCEPTABLE
      "Is this acceptable?",

      Rem 147  OGRE_FULL
      "The ogre doesn't appear to be hungry.",

      Rem 148  OGRE_DODGE
          "The ogre, who despite his bulk is quite agile, easily dodges your\n"
        & "attack.  He seems almost amused by your puny effort.",

      Rem 149  OGRE_PANIC1
          "The ogre, distracted by your rush, is struck by the knife.  With a\n"
        & "blood-curdling yell he turns and bounds after the curmudgeons, who\n"
        & "flee in panic.  You are left alone in the room.",

      Rem 150  OGRE_PANIC2
          "The ogre, distracted by your rush, is struck by the knife.  With a\n"
        & "blood-curdling yell he turns and bounds after the curmudgeon, who\n"
        & "flees in panic.  You are left alone in the room.",

      Rem 151  FREE_FLY
      "The bird flies about agitatedly for a moment.",

      Rem 152  CAGE_FLY
      "The bird flies agitatedly about the cage.",

      Rem 153  NECKLACE_FLY
          "The bird flies about agitatedly for a moment, then disappears through\n"
        & "the crack.  It reappears shortly, carrying in its beak a jade\n"
        & "necklace, which it drops at your feet.",

      Rem 154  WATER_URN
          "You empty the bottle into the urn, which promptly ejects the water\n"
        & "with uncanny accuracy, squirting you directly between the eyes.",

      Rem 155  OIL_URN
      "Your bottle is now empty and the urn is full of oil.",

      Rem 156  FULL_URN
      "The urn is already full of oil.",

      Rem 157  URN_NOPOUR
      "There's no way to get the oil out of the urn.",

      Rem 158  URN_NOBUDGE
      "The urn is far too firmly embedded for your puny strength to budge it.",

      Rem 159  URN_GENIES
          "As you rub the urn, there is a flash of light and a genie appears.\n"
        & "His aspect is stern as he advises: \"One who wouldst traffic in\n"
        & "precious stones must first learn to recognize the signals thereof.\"\n"
        & "He wrests the urn from the stone, leaving a small cavity.  Turning to\n"
        & "face you again, he fixes you with a steely eye and intones: \"Caution!\"\n"
        & "Genie and urn vanish in a cloud of amber smoke.  The smoke condenses\n"
        & "to form a rare amber gemstone, resting in the cavity in the rock.",

      Rem 160  DOUGHNUT_HOLES
      "I suppose you collect doughnut holes, too?",

      Rem 161  GEM_FITS
      "The gem fits easily into the cavity.",

      Rem 162  RUG_RISES
      "The Persian rug stiffens and rises a foot or so off the ground.",

      Rem 163  RUG_WIGGLES
          "The Persian rug draped over your shoulder seems to wriggle for a\n"
        & "moment, but then subsides.",

      Rem 164  RUG_SETTLES
      "The Persian rug settles gently to the ground.",

      Rem 165  RUG_HOVERS
      "The rug hovers stubbornly where it is.",

      Rem 166  RUG_NOTHING1
      "The rug does not appear inclined to cooperate.",

      Rem 167  RUG_NOTHING2
          "If you mean to use the Persian rug, it does not appear inclined to\n"
        & "cooperate.",

      Rem 168  FLAP_ARMS
      "Though you flap your arms furiously, it is to no avail.",

      Rem 169  RUG_GOES
          "You board the Persian rug, which promptly whisks you across the chasm.\n"
        & "You have time for a fleeting glimpse of a two thousand foot drop to a\n"
        & "mighty river; then you find yourself on the other side.",

      Rem 170  RUG_RETURNS
      "The rug ferries you back across the chasm.",

      Rem 171  ALL_SILENT
      "All is silent.",

      Rem 172  STREAM_GURGLES
      "The stream is gurgling placidly.",

      Rem 173  WIND_WHISTLES
      "The wind whistles coldly past your ears.",

      Rem 174  STREAM_SPLASHES
      "The stream splashes loudly into the pool.",

      Rem 175  NO_MEANING
      "You are unable to make anything of the splashing noise.",

      Rem 176  MURMURING_SNORING
          "You can hear the murmuring of the beanstalks and the snoring of the\n"
        & "curmudgeons.",

      Rem 177  SNAKES_HISSING
      "A loud hissing emanates from the snake pit.",

      Rem 178  DULL_RUMBLING
      "The air is filled with a dull rumbling sound.",

      Rem 179  LOUD_ROAR
      "The roar is quite loud here.",

      Rem 180  TOTAL_ROAR
      "The roaring is so loud that it drowns out all other sound.",

      Rem 181  BIRD_CRAP
          "The bird eyes you suspiciously and flutters away.  A moment later you\n"
        & "feel something wet land on your head, but upon looking up you can see\n"
        & "no sign of the culprit.",

      Rem 182  FEW_DROPS
      "There are only a few drops--not enough to carry.",

      Rem 183  NOT_BRIGHT
      "(Uh, y'know, that wasn't very bright.)",

      Rem 184  TOOK_LONG
      "It's a pity you took so long about it.",

      Rem 185  UPSTREAM_DOWNSTREAM
      "Upstream or downstream?",

      Rem 186  FOREST_QUERY
      "",

      Rem 187  WATERS_CRASHING
      "The waters are crashing loudly against the shore.",

      Rem 188  THROWN_KNIVES
      "%d of them throw knives at you!",

      Rem 189  MULTIPLE_HITS
      "%d of them get you!",

      Rem 190  ONE_HIT
      "One of them gets you!",

      Rem 191  NONE_HIT
      "None of them hits you!",

      Rem 192  DONT_KNOW
      "Sorry, I don't know the word \"%s\".",

      Rem 193  WHAT_DO
      "What do you want to do with the %s?",

      Rem 194  NO_SEE
      "I see no %s here.",

      Rem 195  DO_WHAT
      "%s what?",

      Rem 196  OKEY_DOKEY
      "Okay, \"%s\".",

      Rem 197  GARNERED_POINTS
      "You have garnered %d out of a possible %d points, using %d turn%S.",

      Rem 198  SUSPEND_WARNING
          "I can suspend your Adventure for you so that you can resume later, but\n"
        & "it will cost you 5 points.",

      Rem 199  HINT_COST
      "I am prepared to give you a hint, but it will cost you %d point%S.",

      Rem 200  TOTAL_SCORE
      "You scored %d out of a possible %d, using %d turn%S.",

      Rem 201  NEXT_HIGHER
      "To achieve the next higher rating, you need %d more point%S.",

      Rem 202  NO_HIGHER
          "To achieve the next higher rating would be a neat trick!\n"
        & "Congratulations!!",

      Rem 203  OFF_SCALE
      "You just went off my scale!!",

      Rem 204  SAVERESUME_DISABLED
      "Save and resume are disabled.",

      Rem 205  RESUME_HELP
      "To resume your Adventure, start a new game and then say \"RESUME\".",

      Rem 206  RESUME_ABANDON
      "To resume an earlier Adventure, you must abandon the current one.",

      Rem 207  BAD_SAVE
      "Oops, that does not look like a valid save file.",

      Rem 208  VERSION_SKEW
          "I'm sorry, but that Adventure was begun using Version %d.%d of the\n"
        & "save file format, and this program uses Version %d.%d.  You must find an instance\n"
        & "using that other version in order to resume that Adventure.",

      Rem 209  SAVE_TAMPERING
          "A dark fog creeps in to surround you.  From somewhere in the fog you\n"
        & "hear a stern voice.  \"This Adventure has been tampered with!  You have\n"
        & "been dabbling in magic, knowing not the havoc you might cause thereby.\n"
        & "Leave at once, before you do irrevocable harm!\"  The fog thickens,\n"
        & "until at last you can see nothing at all.  Your vision then clears,\n"
        & "and you find yourself back in The Real World.",

      Rem 210  TWIST_TURN
          "Sorry, but the path twisted and turned so much that I can't figure\n"
        & "out which way to go to get back.",

      Rem 211  GO_UNNEEDED
          "You don't have to say \"go\" every time; just specify a direction or, if\n"
        & "it's nearby, name the place to which you wish to move.",

      Rem 212  NUMERIC_REQUIRED
      "This command requires a numeric argument."

    }

Def MsgNoMessage() As Number
    0

Def MsgCaveNearby() As Number
    1

Def MsgCurmudgeonBlock() As Number
    2

Def MsgCurmudgeonRan() As Number
    3

Def MsgCurmudgeonPack() As Number
    4

Def MsgCurmudgeonSingle() As Number
    5

Def MsgKnifeThrown() As Number
    6

Def MsgSaysPlugh() As Number
    7

Def MsgGetsYou() As Number
    8

Def MsgMissesYou() As Number
    9

Def MsgUnsureFacing() As Number
    10

Def MsgNoInoutHere() As Number
    11

Def MsgCantApply() As Number
    12

Def MsgAmGame() As Number
    13

Def MsgNoMoreDetail() As Number
    14

Def MsgPitchDark() As Number
